it's very  gloomy very strange very trippy very  grotesque i really like a lot of the  nightmare images they're very it's you  know it's weird like fisheye lenses and  [ __ ] like it feels like you're you've  been dosed or something like that so uh  you know it's not a traditional or by  the numbers type of giallo movie so  don't expect the usual hallmarks like i  said like the mass killer and  like the kind of police procedural  aspect because it doesn't really have  that but it's definitely unique although  you know like i said it's on the fringes  of giallo it's usually called a giallo  movie and it is but it's kind of like an  outlier i guess because it's not exactly  like a classic example of the genre that  said i wouldn't hesitate to recommend it  not only to people that are really into  jello movies like me but also to fans of  those sort of like 70s era satanic panic  uh you know cult movies like the ones  that came about uh after rosemary's baby  ones like that  if you like that kind of stuff and you  like stuff with like really surrealistic  or trippy visuals then you'll probably  dig this one as well so that will do it  for this flickers of fear continuing on  with giallo july we'll do another one  next time and i will see you on that one  bye
 

